{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_quorum_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id='b5382a9e45384354ae2bb134e74ae95b',rationale='Review the actual fixed quorum check against its version-1 obligation and completed clean-copy measurements, preserving the modeled-storage and checkpoint scope.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['S_append_duty','S_async_contract','S_joint','S_majority','S_reset_append','S_send','S_leader_ack','S_tracker_commit','S_log_decision','S_bootstrap_api','S_raw_entry','S_ready_advance','S_memory_read_write','S_memory_append','S_log_apply'],rationale='The answering artifact is b5382a9e45384354ae2bb134e74ae95b version 1, executed as b617d2d55bac4add81288c1f82e19cd0; its fixed plan/harness and claim C_append_completed_quorum version 1 were inspected together. The documented duty in S_append_duty is persistence before counting entries toward commitment; S_async_contract assigns append completion before attached-response delivery to the caller. The fixed three-voter majority, with no outgoing voters, follows S_joint/S_majority. This supports the one-way commitment-implies-completed-majority obligation, not an equality or a deadline for commitment. RawNode, rather than Node, is the selected API. The harness serializes calls on one goroutine, constructs empty stores, Bootstraps actual peers, campaigns node 1, and processes actual Ready/local responses to reach a stored, committed and applied prefix at index 4. It then Proposes the actual payload at index 5, term 2. No critical raft or tracker fields are assigned. Append work is FIFO and retained while blocked; each processed message performs MemoryStorage.Append and any SetHardState before releasing its actual Responses. Apply work uses actual MsgStorageApply entries and applies bootstrap configuration entries through ApplyConfChange. No Advance is called in async mode. These inputs establish one legal no-crash modeled-storage history, not disconnected fragments. The four phase_admitted records precede distinct quorum_observed records, correlated by the independent request/phase pair. Index 5 and term 2 remain identical throughout. prefix_complete and proposal_accepted are emitted only after the corresponding runtime checks and successful calls; result fields are not used as prerequisites or applicability filters. The result computes committed from the implementation commit index, and append_completed_majority from separate per-voter MemoryStorage reads matching target term and payload. Match is diagnostic only, so the oracle does not assume the fact being tested. The actual observations are: stored copies 0,1,2,3; commit indexes 4,4,5,5; leader Match 4,4,4,5; leader application 4,4,4,5. At the two-follower checkpoint storage_last=[4,5,5] and Match=[4,5,5] distinguish a valid remote majority from leader-local persistence. The fixed scheduler terminates on exhaustion of permitted work rather than waiting for a comparison to pass, and all four comparisons plus history_finished were emitted. The parser reports no errors, no missing results, and per-result admission matches at indices 38/42/47/60 for results 41/46/59/67. Thus the bounded holds measurement corresponds to the stated necessity condition; the remote-majority phase also supplies an observed permitted path, not an inferred general sufficiency theorem. No issue was found in correspondence within this artifact scope.',counterevidence=[],limitations=['MemoryStorage models the stable-storage completion interface; this execution does not demonstrate disk durability, crash atomicity or recovery after power loss.','Four checkpoints in one fresh-entry, fixed-three-voter, single-term schedule were measured; neither intermediate transitions nor other schedules are claimed exhaustively checked.','The remote-majority control completed in this schedule. No general liveness bound follows, and an uncommitted minority is permitted.','Leader application remaining at 4 before its local completion is a diagnostic observation; this artifact has no independent application-order obligation.','No client-visible loss, general consensus safety proof, membership-transition result or old-term response result follows.'])],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['2ac3304feb4d421c9858c2c7fd602e55','b617d2d55bac4add81288c1f82e19cd0','S_leader_other','S_read_tracking','S_restore_config'],answered='Execution b617d2d55bac4add81288c1f82e19cd0 measured the implication at all four declared checkpoints. A single completed follower did not commit the new entry; two completed followers did commit it with the leader append still pending; final leader completion advanced its application. This answers the accepted fresh-entry support-consumption discriminator within the modeled-storage scope, subject to controller correspondence assessment.',remaining=['ReadOnlySafe accumulated heartbeat acknowledgments across applied voter changes remain an independent source-grounded surface.','Physical crash/restart durability and client-visible consequences remain excluded from this result.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='The local self-support schedule distinguishes the two relevant branches and contains no evidence requiring another variant of the same premise. Next investigate how pending read authority support is consumed when switchToConfig changes voter sets; reuse the existing quorum/configuration map but determine the read contract and actual producer history before assigning an obligation.',question_updates={'b850d5c9ec604b71bcd66608c760f541':{'unknowns':[],'resume_conditions':[]}}))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-quorum-review.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_quorum_review.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_19-39-39-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission-quorum-review.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
